<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newchar_common.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newcharbionics.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="newcharbionics">
    <!-- Tier 4 screen #4 (new-character creator): the BIONICS tab (set_bionics).
         After UI_designs/02_cybernetics_terminal.png — implant lists on the left, a body
         diagram on the right with a slot box per region wired to a bus rail.

         The lists are the SHARED row-list vocabulary (newchar_common.rcss): columns of
         single-line rows whose cells — cursor, checkbox, cost tag, name — line up into
         micro-columns. Same anatomy as TRAITS, which shares this step's point budget.

         The chassis is this step's own: it answers "where does this go", which is the one
         fact a bionic has that a trait does not, and it carries the scan sweep that gives
         the screen its motion. See plans/charcreation-bionics-chassis.md.

         Keyboard: LEFT/RIGHT change column, UP/DOWN move within it, CONFIRM installs or
         removes, RANDOMIZE, REROLL_*, NEXT/PREV_TAB, QUIT. Mouse: row selects, the
         checkbox toggles. -->
    <div class="panel nc-panel">
        <div class="nc-steps">
            <div class="nc-step" data-for="t : tabs"
                 data-class-selected="t.selected" data-class-done="t.done">
                <div class="nc-step-icon" data-style-decorator="t.icon_dec"></div>
                <span class="nc-step-label" data-rml="t.name_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-shell">
            <!-- Navigators. Shortcut text comes from the real binding via
                 input_context::get_desc, so it stays correct after a rebind. -->
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-prev" data-if="has_prev"
                 data-event-click="on_prev()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#60;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="prev_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="prev_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_prev"></div>
            <div class="nc-stage">
                <!-- Meta bar: pools on the left, the point budget on the right, dotted
                     rules above and below it as in the reference. -->
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <div class="nc-meta">
                    <span class="nc-meta-pool" data-rml="points_rml"></span>
                    <span class="nc-meta-budget" data-rml="budget_rml"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <!-- Own row, not inside .nc-meta: at 340dp wedged between the points and
                     budget lines the scale read as clutter rather than as an indicator. It
                     is the one screen-level readout of both sides of the budget, and it is
                     the SAME budget the TRAITS step spends. -->
                <div class="nc-balance-row" data-if="balance.show">
                    <!-- No absolute positioning anywhere: RmlUi resolved `position: absolute`
                         against .nc-panel rather than against .nc-scale's `position: relative`,
                         which put the beam ~39dp above the pans and across the top bar. Pure
                         flow instead: arm row (pan | beam | pan) with the fulcrum beneath. -->
                    <div class="nc-scale">
                        <div class="nc-scale-arm">
                            <div class="nc-scale-pan" data-style-top="balance.good_top">
                                <div class="nc-scale-icon" data-style-decorator="balance.good_icon"></div>
                                <span class="nc-scale-num" data-rml="balance.good_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="nc-scale-beam" data-style-transform="balance.rotate"></div>
                            <div class="nc-scale-pan" data-style-top="balance.bad_top">
                                <span class="nc-scale-num" data-rml="balance.bad_rml"></span>
                                <div class="nc-scale-icon" data-style-decorator="balance.bad_icon"></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-scale-fulcrum" data-style-decorator="balance.fulcrum_icon"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="nc-cols">
                    <!-- Columns are written out rather than generated, because each needs a
                         stable id for C++ to scroll its own cursor into view. The third is
                         for zero-point implants, which only a mod supplies. -->
                    <div class="nc-colwrap">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col0.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col0.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-col0" class="nc-list">
                            <div class="item nc-row" data-for="r, ri : col0.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(0, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-cell-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(0, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-colwrap">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col1.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col1.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-col1" class="nc-list">
                            <div class="item nc-row" data-for="r, ri : col1.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(1, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-cell-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(1, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule" data-if="show_col2"></div>
                    <div class="nc-colwrap" data-if="show_col2">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col2.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col2.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="nc-col2" class="nc-list">
                            <div class="item nc-row" data-for="r, ri : col2.rows"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected" data-class-header="r.header"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(2, ri)">
                                <span class="nc-cell-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-check" data-rml="r.check_rml"
                                      data-event-click="on_check(2, ri)"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-cost" data-rml="r.cost_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <!-- CHASSIS. Six rows of three cells, every position emitted: a junction
                         cell draws the connecting lines and a blank holds its column open, so
                         the grid aligns by flex alone with no pixel arithmetic — the same rule
                         the profession equipment doll and the info-panel notch row follow.

                         A slot box shows the implant occupying the most space in that part,
                         `+N` for any others, and — only when CBM_SLOTS_ENABLED is on, which it
                         is not by default — used/total slots with a capacity bar. The boxes the
                         selected implant would claim take a gold outline, red when it will not
                         fit, so choosing a row is how you learn where it goes.

                         MOTION: a diagnostic pulse runs head to feet down the bus rail, and each
                         row's boxes light a hairline scanline as it passes. One colour per row
                         (`dr.scan_col`) feeds both, so rail and body cannot fall out of step;
                         geometry is newchar_bio_scan.h. Nothing is positioned or transformed —
                         `position: absolute` resolves against .nc-panel in these documents, which
                         is what once put the balance scale's beam through the top bar. -->
                    <div class="nc-bio-chassis">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="chassis_name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="chassis_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="chassis_cap_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-bio-doll">
                            <div class="nc-bio-dollrow" data-for="dr : doll">
                                <!-- Bus rail: a continuous hairline with one node per body row.
                                     The node is what the sweep lights. -->
                                <div class="nc-bio-rail">
                                    <div class="nc-bio-rail-line"></div>
                                    <div class="nc-bio-rail-node"
                                         data-style-background-color="dr.scan_col"></div>
                                    <div class="nc-bio-rail-line"></div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="nc-bio-cell" data-for="s : dr.cells"
                                     data-class-blank="s.blank"
                                     data-class-junction="s.junction"
                                     data-class-filled="s.filled"
                                     data-class-want="s.want"
                                     data-class-over="s.over">
                                    <!-- Three stacked children so the rung lands at the exact
                                         vertical middle from equal flex alone: spine, rung,
                                         spine. It joins the box above to the box below and the
                                         left cell to the right one — no offsets. -->
                                    <div class="nc-bio-spine" data-if="s.junction"></div>
                                    <div class="nc-bio-rung" data-if="s.junction"></div>
                                    <div class="nc-bio-spine" data-if="s.junction"></div>
                                    <div class="nc-bio-slot" data-if="!s.blank && !s.junction">
                                        <div class="nc-bio-scanline"
                                             data-style-background-color="dr.scan_col"></div>
                                        <div class="nc-bio-art" data-style-decorator="s.dec"></div>
                                        <span class="nc-bio-impl" data-rml="s.impl_rml"></span>
                                        <div class="nc-bio-slotfoot">
                                            <span class="nc-bio-part" data-rml="s.name_rml"></span>
                                            <span class="nc-bio-cap" data-rml="s.cap_rml"></span>
                                            <span class="nc-bio-more" data-rml="s.more_rml"></span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="nc-bio-bar" data-if="s.show_cap">
                                            <div class="nc-bio-bar-fill"
                                                 data-style-width="s.bar_w"></div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <!-- ":: BIONIC NAME" over the detail panel, as in the reference. -->
                <div class="nc-selname" data-rml="sel_name_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-info-panel">
                    <!-- Art slot: the CBM's own sprite, not the avatar. The chassis beside the
                         lists already is this screen's body view, and an implant does not change
                         how the character looks. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-art" data-if="has_art"
                         data-style-decorator="art_dec"></div>
                    <div class="nc-info-facts">
                        <div class="nc-fact" data-for="f : facts">
                            <div class="nc-fact-label" data-rml="f.label_rml"></div>
                            <div class="nc-fact-value" data-rml="f.value_rml"></div>
                            <!-- Carries the reason an unavailable implant cannot be installed,
                                 which used to exist only as a popup AFTER pressing CONFIRM. -->
                            <div class="nc-fact-sub" data-rml="f.sub_rml"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Prose in a .nc-info-blurb CHILD: .nc-info-desc is `display: flex`, and a
                         bare text node in a flex container gets no inline context and renders
                         nothing. See plans/charcreation-stats-cards.md. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-desc">
                        <div class="nc-info-blurb" data-rml="desc_rml"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-hint" data-rml="hint_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-next" data-if="has_next"
                 data-event-click="on_next()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#62;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="next_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="next_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_next"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-exit" data-rml="exit_rml"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="crt-overlay" class="crt"></div>
</body>
</rml>
